## The radio room

::bg{location="radio_room" time="morning"}
::music{action="start" mood="peaceful" volume="down"}
@narrator: The radio room smells of warm valves and cold coffee. A man is asleep upright in the operator's chair, headphones around his neck, one hand still on the log.
::use{component="enter" who="sol" side="right"}
@sol{emotion="surprised"}: I'm awake. I was listening with my eyes shut. It's a technique.
@sol{emotion="happy"}: You're the intern. Sol. I do the nights. Nights are when the sky talks.

<branch id="solHello" prompt="He holds out a mug that is definitely not clean.">
  <choice id="coffee" label="Take the coffee anyway">
    ::set{run.aff.sol += 1}
    @sol{emotion="laughing"}: Brave. Ines said you'd be brave or you'd be sensible. I hoped brave.
  </choice>
  <choice id="log" label="Ask what the sky said last night">
    ::set{run.aff.sol += 1}
    @sol{emotion="fond"}: Oh, you actually want to know. Hang on. Nobody asks.
    @sol: Thunder over the Sella at two. A ship off the coast asking for a pressure reading from a mountain it'll never see.
  </choice>
  <choice id="work" label="Say you've got readings to log">
    @sol{emotion="neutral"}: Right. Sure. The log. It's a very good log.
  </choice>
</branch>

@sol: Come up to the roof some night. That's where I actually live.
::auto{character="sol" action="fadeOut"}
